      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right; \"find a hobby\" is a hollow suggestion when the core problem is systemic exhaustion. It's a trap because the system *is* designed to keep you functional, not fulfilled. Instead of trying to find a distraction, perhaps you could look at the *slightest* ways to reclaim a piece of your own time, even if it's just a few minutes of genuine stillness. Sometimes, the smallest acts of defiance against the routine are the most powerful.",
